These reused items give the baseline authority frame and the most direct Vietnamese state-language on Ukraine. I did not reuse the nuclear-specific records because they are off-chapter.

**New evidence**
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Aggression against Ukraine : resolution / adopted by the General Assembly","publisher":"United Nations Digital Library","publication_date":"2022-03-02","url":"https://digitallibrary.un.org/record/3959039","claim":"Viet Nam is listed among the abstentions in the recorded vote on the 2 March 2022 General Assembly resolution on Ukraine.","locator":"vote summary and Viet Nam entry in the recorded vote list","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary UN vote record with explicit vote summary and country-by-country roll call.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"State vote by Viet Nam's UN delegation, not a personal act by Nguyễn Phú Trọng.","contrary_evidence":["An abstention is less forceful than a yes vote.","The record does not identify Trọng personally."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.6","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Nội dung Họp báo thường kỳ lần thứ 3 năm 2022","publisher":"Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Viet Nam","publication_date":"2022-03-03","url":"https://mofa.gov.vn/tin-chi-tiet/chi-tiet/noi-dung-hop-bao-thuong-ky-lan-thu-3-nam-2022--254.html","claim":"Vietnam said it shares ASEAN's position on Ukraine, urged respect for the UN Charter and international law, and called for restraint, an immediate end to force, and renewed dialogue for a long-term peaceful solution.","locator":"Ukraine response section and Q6 response, lines 419-442","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary Vietnamese MFA statement with explicit dated policy language.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"Official state line under Trọng's leadership, but not a direct personal statement by him.","contrary_evidence":["This is a policy stance, not an operational peace-making act.","It shows caution and neutrality, not a firm pro-Ukraine alignment."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.6","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bộ trưởng Bùi Thanh Sơn điện đàm với Bộ trưởng Ngoại giao Liên bang Nga Sergey Lavrov","publisher":"Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Viet Nam","publication_date":"2022-03-16","url":"https://mofa.gov.vn/tin-chi-tiet/chi-tiet/bo-truong-bui-thanh-son-dien-dam-voi-bo-truong-ngoai-giao-lien-bang-nga-sergey-lavrov--163.html","claim":"Vietnam told Russian Foreign Minister Sergey Lavrov that international disputes should be solved peacefully, urged restraint and dialogue, and asked for humanitarian corridors and safe evacuation of civilians, including Vietnamese in Ukraine.","locator":"article body lines 394-403","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary Vietnamese MFA record of a contemporaneous diplomatic call.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"Foreign-minister-level diplomacy within the Trọng-led system, not direct proof of Trọng's personal command.","contrary_evidence":["The call is mediated through the foreign minister, not Trọng himself.","It does not show whether the appeal changed Russian behavior."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.4","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"General Assembly Adopts Text to Suspend Russian Federation from Human Rights Council, Continuing Emergency Special Session on Humanitarian Crisis in Ukraine","publisher":"United Nations Press","publication_date":"2022-04-07","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/ga12414.doc.htm","claim":"Vietnam condemned attacks on civilians in Ukraine and said the only way forward is to resume dialogue to achieve a peaceful settlement.","locator":"statement by the representative of Viet Nam in the meeting record","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary UN meeting coverage quoting the Vietnamese delegate in a formal session record.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"Delegation-level statement, not a personal declaration by Trọng.","contrary_evidence":["Vietnam did not join a more maximal condemnation posture.","The statement stresses procedure and dialogue rather than sanctions or coercion."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.4","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"With 143 Votes in Favour, 5 Against, General Assembly Adopts Resolution Condemning Russian Federation’s Annexation of Four Eastern Ukraine Regions","publisher":"United Nations Press","publication_date":"2022-10-12","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/ga12458.doc.htm","claim":"Vietnam said it was following the Ukraine war with concern, called for immediate cessation of hostilities and de-escalation, and emphasized civilian and infrastructure protection.","locator":"statement by Dang Hoang Giang in the meeting record","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary UN meeting coverage with a named Vietnamese representative and a precise date.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"Delegation-level statement under Vietnam's leadership, not direct personal conduct by Trọng.","contrary_evidence":["Again, this is diplomatic language rather than direct enforcement.","Vietnam abstained earlier in the year instead of voting yes on the first Ukraine resolution."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.4","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Vietnam party chief to visit China's Xi next week","publisher":"Reuters via Euronews","publication_date":"2022-10-26","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/10/26/china-vietnam","claim":"Reuters reported that Trong would make a rare overseas trip to China, had sent Xi a congratulatory message about strengthening political trust, and that the relationship remains shaped by territorial disputes in the South China Sea.","locator":"lines 657-670","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting, but mediated through Euronews syndication.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Trọng as party chief in foreign relations.","contrary_evidence":["The visit also reflects strategic balancing with China, not only peace-building.","The article highlights unresolved mistrust and territorial disputes."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.3","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Viet Nam, China issue joint statement","publisher":"Viet Nam Government News","publication_date":"2022-11-02","url":"https://en.baochinhphu.vn/viet-nam-china-issue-joint-statement-11122110208592351.htm","claim":"Viet Nam and China agreed to properly handle sea issues through consultation, avoid actions that complicate and expand disputes, and pursue long-term solutions consistent with UNCLOS while maintaining peace and stability in the East Sea.","locator":"paragraphs 232-235 of the joint statement text","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government-issued joint statement from Trọng's official China visit.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"Directly tied to Trọng's official visit and diplomatic posture.","contrary_evidence":["Joint statements are negotiated texts and do not prove later compliance.","The same statement also reflects close party-to-party alignment with China."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.4","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bộ trưởng Bùi Thanh Sơn gặp Bộ trưởng Ngoại giao Ucraina Dmytro Kuleba","publisher":"Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Viet Nam","publication_date":"2022-11-12","url":"https://mofa.gov.vn/tin-chi-tiet/chi-tiet/-bo-truong-bui-thanh-son-gap-bo-truong-ngoai-giao-ucraina-dmytro-kuleba--139.html","claim":"Vietnam said it values its traditional friendship and comprehensive partnership with Ukraine, and both sides agreed to resume political consultations and intergovernmental talks while the conflict was affecting bilateral cooperation.","locator":"article body lines 408-411","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary Vietnamese MFA meeting record with named counterparts and dated diplomatic follow-up.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"State diplomacy under Trọng's leadership, not personal military conduct.","contrary_evidence":["This is relationship maintenance, not conflict resolution power.","It does not show Vietnam had leverage to end the war."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ambassadors in Vietnam call on Hanoi to support Ukraine amid Russia’s invasion","publisher":"Radio Free Asia","publication_date":"2022-03-10","url":"https://www.rfa.org/english/news/vietnam/ambassadors-op-ed-03102022164041.html","claim":"Twenty-two ambassadors in Vietnam publicly urged Hanoi to support Ukraine after the abstention and argued that neutrality would not serve legal or humanitarian interests.","locator":"headline, dek, and paragraphs 49-67","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Timely and explicit, but it is an advocacy op-ed rather than a primary fact record.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly in 2022","ruler_attribution":"External criticism of Viet Nam's state stance, not direct evidence of Trọng's personal decision-making.","contrary_evidence":["It is opinionated diplomatic pressure, not a legal finding.","It does not prove that a different vote was available or would have changed events."],"lenses":["2B.6","2B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I screened roughly 30 documents and kept 9 new URLs plus 2 reused items.

Kept because they were directly claim-bearing and 2022-relevant:
- UN voting record for the March 2 Ukraine resolution
- Vietnamese MFA briefing on Ukraine
- Vietnamese MFA call with Russian FM
- UN meeting records on April 7 and October 12
- Reuters reporting on Trọng's China visit
- The Vietnam-China joint statement
- Vietnamese MFA meeting with the Ukrainian FM
- RFA criticism of Hanoi's abstention

Rejected or not retained:
- Duplicate Reuters syndications and secondary rewrites of the same Vietnam-China or Ukraine stories
- Generic UN document indexes that did not add a claim beyond the retained vote record
- Later 2023-2026 material that was outside the 2022 target period
- Broad human-rights or peacekeeping pages that did not speak to 2B conduct by the ruler
- Items that were too indirect, repetitive, or purely background

**Remaining gaps**
- There is still no direct evidence that Nguyễn Phú Trọng personally initiated, escalated, or managed any interstate use of force in 2022.
- Proxy conduct, arms transfers, and accountability for military failures are essentially absent, which is expected for Vietnam in this period but still leaves 2B.5 and 2B.9 thin.
- Most positive evidence is state- and delegation-level diplomacy rather than a personal command decision by Trọng.
- More search would mainly help if you want deeper archival proof of CPV Politburo or defense-council involvement in foreign/security policy; it is unlikely to change the basic picture that 2022 shows restraint and dialogue, not war-making.
